  "output": "{\"score\":8,\"findings\":[{\"file\":\"plugins/agent/impact/plugin.sh\",\"category\":\"logic\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"line\":617,\"message\":\"The v2 merge on the success path has a silent fallback (else branch, line 621) that writes the raw LLM impact_json without result_contract, disposition, or reason when jq fails; _IMPACT_RESULT_WRITTEN=1 is set either way so no second write opportunity exists, meaning a jq failure silently produces a v1-shaped artifact from a manifest that declares result_contract:2 — the engine would apply v1 control flow to what was intended as a v2 result.\",\"introduced\":true},{\"file\":\"plugins/agent/impact/plugin.sh\",\"category\":\"logic\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"line\":426,\"message\":\"The disposition default ':-interrupted' (line 426 and 431) is used when router_reason_disposition returns empty; the current implementation never returns empty for a non-empty reason (has a catch-all), but if router_reason_disposition is extended and gains a new reason it does not recognise, or if the sourcing of router-rc-classify.sh fails silently (no set -e in the sourced library context), all unclassified router failures would default to disposition=interrupted (retryable) rather than the correct halting disposition, making a config or infra error look like a transient retry.\",\"introduced\":true},{\"file\":\"plugins/agent/impact/plugin.sh\",\"category\":\"logic\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"line\":416,\"message\":\"When _router_rc_classify returns _rc_verdict='fail' (rc=2 router_config_error, or any unrecognised rc → router_rc_nonzero), the condition '_rc_verdict == error' is false so _out_verdict becomes 'incomplete'; the v2 disposition (misconfigured or unavailable) does cause the engine to halt correctly, but the verdict and disposition are semantically contradictory — a cycle orchestrator that reads verdict independently of disposition would interpret 'incomplete' as re-iterate; this behaviour was pre-existing in the v1 code and is not worsened, but the v2 migration did not correct it.\",\"introduced\":false},{\"file\":\"tests/unit/impact-no-path-construction-test.sh\",\"category\":\"coverage\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"line\":28,\"message\":\"SPEC-8's grep patterns match bare-variable forms (artifacts_dir/design.md, $state_dir/...) but do not match brace-quoted forms (${artifacts_dir}/design.md), leaving a gap already noted by the spec-correspondence stage; a future refactor that introduces brace-quoted path constructions would pass the test while violating the SPEC.\",\"introduced\":true}]}",
